  "interpretation": "Split result. The multigrid V-cycle achieves the property it was built for: the average residual reduction per cycle is 0.487-0.537 across a 12.7x range in unknowns, flat to 10%. The outer Krylov iteration count is not flat -- 94 to 230, a 2.45x growth over that same 12.7x -- so the route is not h-independent in the sense the benchmark's own docstring requires of it. Growth is sublinear rather than proportional. The measured advantage is memory: every rung converged to a true relative residual of 1e-10, including 614,656 unknowns at 1.08 GB, past the ~488,000 where the classical route is recorded as running out of memory.",
